Sigh. Went into the Rogue quest unspoiled and discovered what so many have
learned before me: don't go there without level-teleporting or polymorphing
ability. Apart from that unfortunate sex-change operation, Rufus was my
very first serious attempt at a Rogue and she was doing so well, too.
Suppose she might get lucky and someone could turn up with the right kind
of potion before she starves, but I'm not holding my breath.

This one bugs me. I accept that NetHack is a dangerous game, and that
mortal peril lurks around every corner, but setting up a situation where
the first time through an unspoiled character is almost certain to die is..
annoying. The DevTeam should do this differently, even if it's just adding
a small cryptic warning somewhere. Maybe have a special Oracle message for
Rogues? (Or does something already exist and I missed it?) Or maybe include
one hidden level-teleport trap in each of the walled-off sections which is
invariably set to dump you in some unhelpful location. All the way back up
on level one, or directly into Medusa's moat? At least then you don't have
to sit around and wait to starve.

On the other hand, it *was* a nice change of pace that the rogue Quest
Leader treats you like dirt, and the city of Ramwhosis was nicely designed. 

And in a general sense, the use of a lot of traps is appropriate. I
wouldn't change that. 

Ah, well. Thanks for letting me vent. Back in the saddle; Rufus must be
avenged...



